[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1477","stub":{"id":"1477","section":"1. Pioneer Mill Dam in Tiffin to CR 38","altname":"Huss Street Wave Section","river":"Sandusky","difficulty":"III","states":["USA-OHI"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"low-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"1200","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":"II"},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Put in at Nature Trails Park: **220 E Davis St, Tiffin, OH 44883**\n\nGPS Coordinates for River Access Parking: **41.1262382558504, -83.16870125127963**","id":"111110","location":{"latitude":"41.12606915","longitude":"-83.16858905"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0.02","photoID":"hMkrkI8LELAZy9xStJGI8","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"At high water, there's some gentle surf waves to warm up on.","id":"KaOhDgp9WzLlaaMwmgLY8","location":{"latitude":"41.1266254","longitude":"-83.1670961"},"name":"Warm-up Waves","distance":"0.1","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"GTUycXOg6ALYKDbX30qEp"},{"type":"hazard","description":"This feature is formed by a broken dam near Huss Street and offers dynamic paddling conditions across a wide range of water levels. At **low flows**, it provides fun eddies and playful hydraulics. Around **5.5 ft (4000 CFS)**, the central hydraulic becomes deep and powerful—if you hit it head-on, it will likely flip you, but it won’t hold you once you’re upside down. As the river rises to around **6.5 ft (6000 CFS)**, the rapid transforms into a large, glassy surf wave that forms on the tongue of current flowing through the broken section of the dam. This wave is local favorite park-and-play spot during wet springs.\n\nOnly the **river right side** of the dam was removed. The **river left half remains intact**, creating changing dynamics as levels increase:\n\n- **Below 5 ft (3500 CFS)**: Water flows through the broken section.\n- **Above 5 ft (3500 CFS)**: Water begins spilling over the remaining low-head dam.\n- **At 6 ft and up (5000 CFS)**: The intact portion becomes increasingly **retentive and hazardous**.\n\n### High Water Navigation\n\nAt high flows, start **right of center** as you approach Huss Street. Your target is the gap **between the two bridge supports**. Once committed to the rapid, you'll spot the line: a **diagonal move from right of center toward the left corner of the hydraulic**.\n\n### Hazards\n\n- **Wood** commonly gets caught on the **river right bridge support** and may require removal.\n- **River left support** generally stays clear.\n\n### Pro Tip\n\n**Scout from the bridge above** when levels are high—it’s the best way to evaluate the current line and assess wood or other hazards before committing.","id":"6r8etpAbY2fxjz2W0gmMp","location":{"latitude":"41.1306232","longitude":"-83.16596981"},"name":"Huss Street Rapid","distance":"0.39","photoID":"jomiHSTVGzVJQ14BhRBzv","difficulty":"III","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"On river right, near the houses, there’s an excellent surf wave that becomes a local favorite at the right levels. While it can be tricky to catch due to limited eddy service, once you’re in, the ride is smooth and rewarding. The wave sits next to Rivers Edge Executive Suites, where guests often watch from the shore—giving you the perfect audience to show off your super skills and be the star of the show.","id":"KpDWhdimHgs0pvNUfAlAG","location":{"latitude":"41.1433562","longitude":"-83.15814152"},"name":"Superstar","distance":"1.38","difficulty":"III-","approximate":false,"photoID":"pEVmIbXhPoOkSd2jTGB7I"},{"type":"takeout","description":"The take-out is a small river access point located at: **3408 N County Rd 33, Tiffin, OH 44883**\n\nIf you're not familiar with the area, it may look like just a roadside pull-off—keep an eye out so you don’t miss it!\n\nGPS Coordinates for River Access: **41.16864616328115, -83.16254382147336**","id":"116378","location":{"latitude":"41.1676712","longitude":"-83.16323853"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"3.5","photoID":"pdxZ6AQQv1m78nJWAo8Ts","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"36Y0dioIHRUZu2Cf0jlX0","ext":"jpg","post_id":"CT69eUo2almwQIHQRjgzg","description":"at 2,000 CFS","caption":"The end of Bend","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Domenic Bentz","poi_id":"1ep1qKKvclHD7euD6eUTz","photo_date":"2025-08-02T01:36:03.000Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T01:36:03.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/36Y0dioIHRUZu2Cf0jlX0","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/36Y0dioIHRUZu2Cf0jlX0"}},{"id":"1340","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3031","description":"","caption":"Jeff and Steve","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1340","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1340"}},{"id":"PfjPVdAdrtIvo9zMLlU4P","ext":"jpg","post_id":"j5EQ30FDY9V4LA2wwWTrK","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Domenic Bentz","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-08-02T01:14:05.000Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T01:14:05.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/PfjPVdAdrtIvo9zMLlU4P","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/PfjPVdAdrtIvo9zMLlU4P"}},{"id":"hMkrkI8LELAZy9xStJGI8","ext":"jpg","post_id":"MUQn9GAP4NNTedvbAp0ax","description":"","caption":"Put-In photo sized for this webiste","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Domenic Bentz","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-08-02T01:18:40.000Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T01:18:40.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/hMkrkI8LELAZy9xStJGI8","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/hMkrkI8LELAZy9xStJGI8"}},{"id":"jomiHSTVGzVJQ14BhRBzv","ext":"jpg","post_id":"CT69eUo2almwQIHQRjgzg","description":"at 2,000 CFS","caption":"Huss St R